        "stageRecord": "The sentence contains a Swedish bli-passive: läst is the passive participle, and av Sara identifies the reader. The participle first combines with Boken in its complement position, where the noun phrase receives the Theme role. The av-phrase is right-adjoined to the participial V′ and realizes the passive predicate's Agent; it is not an ordinary direct object. Passive participial morphology suppresses structural accusative assignment, so Boken cannot receive Case in this position. A classical GB analysis with NP arguments is adopted: Boken is an already inflected definite noun, and its suffix is not represented as a separate syntactic terminal. The finite passive auxiliary blev is introduced separately as a verbal head; its projection and subsequent raising are constructed in later stages.",
