        "stageRecord": "The auxiliary selects the previously constructed participial VP and projects an upper VP. Abstract finite past I is then introduced above that VP. Boken moves from the participle's complement position to Spec-IP, leaving an NP trace in its original position. This is A-movement: the passive auxiliary introduces no competing external argument, and Spec-IP supplies no new theta role. The resulting chain retains the Theme role assigned at its foot, while finite I licenses nominative at its head. This satisfies the Case Filter and the requirement for a clausal subject. The analysis uses trace representations, not silent lexical copies. Blev remains in its verbal base position at this stage; the abstract I head is unpronounced and is not a separately pronounced tense suffix.",
        "statement": "Project the auxiliary and finite clause, and raise Boken to the subject position.",
