        "stageRecord": "A matrix declarative CP is projected above IP. The complex finite I head raises to C, leaving an I trace; Boken then moves from the already established Spec-IP position to Spec-CP, leaving a subject trace. This is the CP analysis of Swedish verb-second order: the initial subject occupies the preverbal field, and blev occupies C. The subject's A′-movement does not add a theta role or a new Case requirement; its nominative and Theme dependencies remain mediated by its A-position and original complement position. The head chain passes through I rather than crossing it, and the nominal dependency stays within one clause without crossing an island. The passive Agent is realized by av Sara, and läst is compatible with the singular common-gender subject. The completed structure therefore licenses the exact input as grammatical, meaning that the book was read by Sara. Subject-initial V2 is represented uniformly here; this does not require contrastive topic emphasis. The overt terminals, with all traces and abstract heads silent, yield Boken blev läst av Sara.",
        "statement": "Complete the grammatical Swedish V2 declarative.",
